[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Kibana 6.8.23 runs here on the Node.js 24 of www/node24 (it was made for
Node.js 10): %%WWWDIR%%/src/setup_node_env/node_compat.js puts back
what it needs of Node.js 10, hapi has its fixes for Node.js 16, and re2 is
node-re2 1.27.1 built for this Node.js.

Machine Learning and Reporting (with its CSV export) are off: Elasticsearch has
no machine learning on FreeBSD, and Reporting needs the Chromium or PhantomJS
of Kibana, which FreeBSD cannot run and the package does not have. They are off
in %%ETCDIR%%/kibana.yml.sample and, for an older kibana.yml too, by the rc
script (kibana_args in rc.conf). The bundles of the package are built for these
plugins: with another set (a plugin turned on or off, one installed) Kibana
builds them again in %%WWWDIR%%/optimize at its start, which takes
minutes and more than 1 GB of memory.

service kibana reload opens the log file again (after its rotation).
EOM
}
]
